Who has achieved a top six running back standing

505
00:22:08,740 --> 00:22:09,859
Like I mentioned moments ago

506
00:22:09,859 --> 00:22:11,220
In back-to-back seasons

507
00:22:11,220 --> 00:22:14,099
And has been top seven in fantasy points per touch

508
00:22:14,099 --> 00:22:16,019
In the last two seasons

509
00:22:16,099 --> 00:22:20,660
So why do I believe that Devon H&N is going to take a little bit of a slide in 2026

510
00:22:20,660 --> 00:22:23,940
Well it primarily revolves around so many changes within this offense

511
00:22:23,940 --> 00:22:25,380
Like I mentioned previously

512
00:22:25,380 --> 00:22:27,859
In the last 25 games with a healthy two of Tonga Biloa

513
00:22:27,859 --> 00:22:30,579
He was averaging 6.08 targets per game

514
00:22:30,579 --> 00:22:34,180
Which led to 8.89 fantasy points per game

515
00:22:34,180 --> 00:22:37,460
From receiving statistics isolated over those 25 games

516
00:22:37,460 --> 00:22:40,660
So when we go ahead and potentially impact the receiving utilization

517
00:22:40,660 --> 00:22:42,900
Again that is going to reduce the fantasy point upside

518
00:22:42,900 --> 00:22:45,140
He can maintain in 2026

519
00:22:45,220 --> 00:22:47,460
You have a new starting quarterback in Malik Willis

520
00:22:47,460 --> 00:22:49,940
Who over the course of the last two seasons

521
00:22:49,940 --> 00:22:50,980
When he has played

522
00:22:50,980 --> 00:22:53,460
He has had an 8.9% check down rate

523
00:22:53,460 --> 00:22:55,859
In comparison to 2 was 15.8%

524
00:22:55,859 --> 00:22:59,059
And has maintained a 19% scramble rate per dropback

525
00:22:59,059 --> 00:23:01,380
Which again does give us cost for concern

526
00:23:01,380 --> 00:23:03,380
In the receiving category of Devon H&N

527
00:23:03,380 --> 00:23:05,539
Now you have a new offensive coordinator in Bobby Slovak

528
00:23:05,539 --> 00:23:07,940
Who of course wants to maintain a run heavy attack

529
00:23:07,940 --> 00:23:09,619
And demonstrated that with Joe Mixon

530
00:23:09,619 --> 00:23:13,700
As the offensive coordinator of the Houston Texans in 2023 and 2024

531
00:23:13,700 --> 00:23:16,259
Again we certainly do believe that Devon H&N

532
00:23:16,259 --> 00:23:17,619
Is still going to be of value

533
00:23:17,619 --> 00:23:21,059
But can a running back of this caliber sustain top 12 upside

534
00:23:21,059 --> 00:23:24,500
While being associated with potentially a bottom five scoring offense

535
00:23:24,500 --> 00:23:26,339
Over the course of the last five seasons

536
00:23:26,339 --> 00:23:28,660
We have only seen five running backs

537
00:23:28,660 --> 00:23:30,980
Achieve top 20 standing at the running back position

538
00:23:30,980 --> 00:23:33,299
While being associated with the bottom five offense

539
00:23:33,299 --> 00:23:36,420
Only twice have we seen them achieve top 12 standing

540
00:23:36,420 --> 00:23:40,420
That's 2023 Bresol and 2023 Sequan Barclay

541
00:23:40,420 --> 00:23:41,539
Certainly going to be difficult

542
00:23:41,539 --> 00:23:43,220
But if anybody can accomplish it

543
00:23:43,299 --> 00:23:44,579
It's going to be Devon H&N

544
00:23:44,579 --> 00:23:46,259
All right, let's close out the top 12 running backs

545
00:23:46,259 --> 00:23:47,779
With of course Kenneth Walker

546
00:23:47,779 --> 00:23:50,819
Kenneth Walker was subjected to nearly a 50-50 split

547
00:23:50,819 --> 00:23:53,460
During his 2025 campaign with Zach Sharbenay

548
00:23:53,460 --> 00:23:56,259
Of course stealing many of his touchdowns and fantasy points

549
00:23:56,259 --> 00:23:57,460
He could have potentially scored

550
00:23:57,460 --> 00:23:58,980
But with the 15 opportunities per game

551
00:23:58,980 --> 00:24:00,579
He was given during the regular season

552
00:24:00,579 --> 00:24:01,539
Which is still brutal

553
00:24:01,539 --> 00:24:04,099
He was solved with nearly 11 fantasy points per game

554
00:24:04,099 --> 00:24:05,460
Then came the Sharbenay injury

